WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.557
OT security monitoring is the continuing observation and analysis of industrial systems, networks, identities, and operational activity for evidence of security-relevant change.

00:00:10.557 --> 00:00:19.766
It helps defenders understand what is communicating, what actions are occurring, and whether current behavior matches the expected operation.

00:00:19.766 --> 00:00:26.729
Visibility may include network conversations among controllers, HMIs, engineering workstations, historians, and remote-access systems.

00:00:26.729 --> 00:00:32.345
It can also include authentication, firewall, endpoint, application, and configuration events.

00:00:32.345 --> 00:00:39.308
No single source provides the complete picture, so monitoring combines evidence from several layers.

00:00:39.308 --> 00:00:45.822
OT monitoring differs from ordinary enterprise monitoring because technical activity has process meaning.

00:00:45.822 --> 00:00:52.335
A command may be expected during a maintenance window and concerning during production.

00:00:52.335 --> 00:00:59.748
A communication loss may represent a cyber event, equipment failure, network fault, or planned shutdown.

00:00:59.748 --> 00:01:05.812
Operators and engineers provide context that security telemetry cannot create by itself.

00:01:05.812 --> 00:01:10.529
Safety, reliability, and availability constrain how monitoring is deployed.

00:01:10.529 --> 00:01:15.246
Active probes and untested agents may disrupt sensitive devices.

00:01:15.246 --> 00:01:21.760
Passive collection and carefully placed sensors are often preferred, especially near control networks.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:28.274
Monitoring should never create an uncontrolled path or a single point of failure.

00:01:28.274 --> 00:01:35.237
The purpose is not to collect every packet forever or generate the most alerts.

00:01:35.237 --> 00:01:43.548
Effective monitoring establishes asset and behavior visibility, detects meaningful deviation, supports investigation, preserves evidence, and informs response.

00:01:43.548 --> 00:01:55.003
It becomes valuable when the organization can explain what an observation means, who reviews it, and what action follows without jeopardizing the physical process.
